<LegalPage eyebrow="Notices" title="Third-Party Licenses" description="Open-source components included in Vector retain their original license terms.">
  <section>
    <h2>Bundled third-party notices</h2>
    <p>These notices are included with Vector. Starting with 1.99.99, desktop and CLI distributions also include DEPENDENCY_NOTICES.md with package versions, license texts, and available copyright notices for bundled and external dependencies. Packages that omit a notice file are identified explicitly.</p>
    <pre>{notices}</pre>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Optional social-card server notices</h2>
    <p>The documentation image service uses separate server components. Their notices and source archive references follow.</p>
    <pre>{socialCardNotices}</pre>
  </section>
  <section><h2>Scope</h2><p>The <a href="/legal/license">Vector Software License</a> applies to Vector-owned code, branding, product assets, and proprietary additions. It does not replace or narrow the permissions attached to third-party code.</p></section>
</LegalPage>
